# AGENT.md — src/

Application root for the Onion Architecture on Fastify.

## What lives here

- `main.ts` — starts the server{{#if hasOrm}} and initializes the ORM connection{{/if}}.
- `app.ts` — composition root. Builds the Fastify instance, registers plugins
  and module routes.
- `config/` — environment loading, swagger setup.
- `errors/` — AppError base class and subclasses (NotFoundError, ValidationError).
- `shared/` — cross-cutting infrastructure (database, cache{{#if useAuth}}, auth{{/if}}{{#if useHealthCheck}}, health{{/if}}).

## Onion Architecture layers

```
src/
├── domain/          ← Innermost: entities, repository interfaces (ports)
├── application/     ← Use cases, DTOs, service implementations
├── infrastructure/  ← Persistence adapters (TypeORM, Prisma, Mongoose, in-memory)
└── presentation/    ← Outermost: Fastify route plugins (export default async function)
```

## Rules

- Do not put business logic in `main.ts` or `app.ts`.
- When you add a new module, register its route plugin in `app.ts` with
  `await fastify.register(moduleRoutes, { prefix: '/name' })`.
- Fastify plugins receive the `FastifyInstance` and register routes with
  `fastify.get()`, `fastify.post()`, etc. — no Router objects like Express.
- Error handler is set globally via `setErrorHandler` in `app.ts`.
{{#if useAuth}}
- Auth works via `@fastify/jwt`. Protected routes call
  `await request.jwtVerify()` or use the `authenticate` decorator.
{{/if}}
